      "note": "The sneaker squeak: rubber sticking and slipping on the lacquer, the slip rate rising as the foot lets go. A voice source used as a friction oscillator (one pulse per slip, so `freq` is the slip rate) through the sole's own narrow resonances; jitter, shimmer and rasp keep it rubbery, not a whistle.",
